{"repositoryId":549243948,"availability":"available","full":"filipecabaco/snowglobe","name":"snowglobe","description":"Package Docker into WASM","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":12,"forks":3,"created":"2022-10-10T22:38:47Z","updated":"2026-10-16T19:43:38Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://filipecabaco.github.io/snowglobe/","topics":[],"demo":"https://filipecabaco.github.io/snowglobe/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:45.911Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:45.911Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:45.911Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T11:02:45.911Z","stars":12,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Package a Docker image into a website that runs it in the browser. snowglobe boots your image on real Linux inside armless, a 64-bit ARM machine compiled to WebAssembly, snapshots it once your app is ready, and writes a folder of static files. Visitors get your program running in their tab in about a second, with no server behind it.","This is an experiment. Everything runs on an emulated 64-bit ARM CPU (translated to WebAssembly as it runs), so expect it to be slower than native. A site can have up to 8 CPUs (--cpus), which helps programs that use them (the Elixir demo runs CPU-bound tasks about 4× faster on 4); the demos use 2, to stay light on phones."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/filipecabaco/snowglobe/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a2d7deceb28c7abbab7d4e9299e38409e860bafa161a26b4701dead3f7f21875","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:46.067Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:46.067Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Package a Docker image into a website that runs it in the browser. snowglobe boots your image on real Linux inside armless, a 64-bit ARM machine compiled to WebAssembly, snapshots it once your app is ready, and writes a folder of static files. Visitors get your program running in their